                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elysian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5598f18f-9f1e-3933-8424-8e115e2ba259",
                                        "entry_id": "b1c33015-b1d8-3a31-9499-9ab5320c0ee6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to Elysian or Elysium, the location."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab604aaf-f07a-45bd-9c23-f263ab278efe",
                                                "sense_id": "5598f18f-9f1e-3933-8424-8e115e2ba259",
                                                "text": "Departed spirits do not however make a joyful and immediate entrance into these elysian fields, but must first slide for the space of five days, or, according to others, for a still longer period, down a rough rock, which the Greenlanders, by a strange contradiction, represent to be quite bloody."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63b6e251-472f-4edf-b002-eba6eaf75e63",
                                                "sense_id": "5598f18f-9f1e-3933-8424-8e115e2ba259",
                                                "text": "But everyone that has lived a wicked life on earth, committed murder in his own nation, or been guilty of suicide, must pass by a different route to the Elysian fields. He has a steep precipice to climb, which gives him much pain and trouble; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bf69ff3-682d-3ad5-9eb3-683742d94869",
                                        "entry_id": "b1c33015-b1d8-3a31-9499-9ab5320c0ee6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Blissful, happy, heavenly"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d0258c8-9946-44dc-9626-e3c6beafd684",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf69ff3-682d-3ad5-9eb3-683742d94869",
                                                "text": "O vvho of man the ſtory vvill unfold, / Ere victory and empire vvrought annoy, / In that elyſian age (miſnamed of gold) / The age of love, and innocence and joy, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcfef107-bb46-4f02-8533-e50d7f63250b",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf69ff3-682d-3ad5-9eb3-683742d94869",
                                                "text": "Unlike Raphael's \"Galatea\" and his \"Three Graces\", examples of Elysian happiness in a race in the state of innocence, Giulio [Romano]'s decorations resemble saturnalia of lubricity itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bfecb29-0e85-4abb-ae2e-761de234ea38",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf69ff3-682d-3ad5-9eb3-683742d94869",
                                                "text": "Mystic waves of beauty blended / With the gorgeous golden rays / Phantasies of bliss descended / In a myrrh'd Elysian haze. / In the lyre-born chords extended / Harmonies of Lydian lays."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94a76e26-9831-4f48-a33e-4f1c5536894e",
                                                "sense_id": "7bf69ff3-682d-3ad5-9eb3-683742d94869",
                                                "text": "Winchester College has an Elysian quality, doubtless appreciated by the classical masters who supplied its educational staple for most of its six-century history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elysian",
